# zfish project files
.zig-cache/
zig-cache/
zig-out/
kcov-out/
__DEV/
__pycache__
.venv
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
uv.lock

# Files from build
**/*.o
**/*.s
.build_sha.txt
.build_date.txt

# resources/ is a scratch directory, not a source directory: every byte in it is fetched
# (`zig build bench` pulls the net, `zig build tb` pulls Syzygy) or dropped there by hand (the
# fastchess binary, its opening book). `.gitkeep` is the ONLY tracked entry, so ignore the
# contents wholesale and re-include it. Listing artifacts one by one is what let a 175 MB
# opening book and a 2.3 MB fastchess binary sit untracked: each new artifact type needed a new
# line and nobody added one. This needs none. To commit something here anyway, `git add -f` --
# and then give it a real home, because nothing else in the tree reads from resources/.
resources/*
!resources/.gitkeep

# Keep these path-independent too: a net or a tablebase can be pointed anywhere via cwd or
# SyzygyPath, so the resources/ rule above is not the only place they can land.
**/*.nnue

# Files generated by the instrumented tests
tsan.supp
__pycache__/
/.zfish-upstream-oracle/

# Syzygy tablebases: pointed at by SyzygyPath, which need not be resources/
*.rtbw
*.rtbz

# fastchess writes this into its CWD on an autosave interval, so a killed Elo run can be
# resumed. It is generated state, not configuration -- it carries the engine paths, the TC and
# the running W/L/D of whatever match last ran.
/config.json
